---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Final from '../components/Final.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site.js';

const seo = {
  title: 'Work With Me: The Self-Led Executive Programme | Alister Gates',
  description: 'A private 3-month IFS-informed coaching programme for founders, CEOs and senior leaders. Ten 90-minute sessions online, fully confidential. Contact me for pricing.',
};

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Service', name: 'The Self-Led Executive programme', serviceType: 'Executive coaching', url: `${SITE}/work-with-me/`,
  description: seo.description, provider: { '@id': `${SITE}/#person` },
  areaServed: ['Europe', 'United Kingdom', 'Switzerland', 'Middle East', 'United States', 'Australia', 'New Zealand'],
};
---
<Base title={seo.title} description={seo.description} schema={schema}>
  <section class="on-dark has-bg">
    <div class="bg" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/man-at-window.webp" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" /></div>
    <div class="wrap section stack wm-hero">
      <p class="label">Work with me</p>
      <h1 class="h1">Three months. <em>One honest look at who's leading.</em></h1>
      <p class="lead">The Self-Led Executive is a private one-to-one programme for founders and senior leaders. It's built around your real week, not a curriculum.</p>
      <p><a class="btn btn--light" href="/contact/">Book a 20-minute call</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap section stack-lg">
      <div class="split">
        <div class="stack"><p class="label">01 — The programme</p><h2 class="h2">What you <em>get.</em></h2></div>
        <div class="split__body"><p>Coaching changes what you do. This changes who's doing it. The structure is simple on purpose, so the time goes into the work.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="cell"><p class="label">Format</p><h3 class="h3">Ten 90-minute sessions.</h3><p>Over three months, one-to-one on video. Weekly to start, then spaced out as the changes settle.</p></div>
        <div class="cell"><p class="label">Focus</p><h3 class="h3">Your real situations.</h3><p>The board, the co-founder, the team, the hard decision, home. We bring IFS to what's actually happening.</p></div>
        <div class="cell"><p class="label">Privacy</p><h3 class="h3">Nothing shared.</h3><p>No reports to your employer or board, no notes passed on. If the company pays, they get an invoice and that's it.</p></div>
        <div class="cell"><p class="label">Capacity</p><h3 class="h3">A small number of clients.</h3><p>I keep this work small, so you get my full attention and sessions at times that suit your time zone.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="tone-stone">
    <div class="wrap section split">
      <div class="stack"><p class="label">02 — The arc</p><h2 class="h2">How the three months <em>usually go.</em></h2></div>
      <div class="split__body">
        <ol class="arc">
          <li><span class="label">Month one</span><span class="arc__title">Map the system.</span><span>We get to know the parts that run you under pressure: what sets them off, what they do and what they're afraid of. Most leaders find this a relief on its own. The pattern finally makes sense.</span></li>
          <li><span class="label">Month two</span><span class="arc__title">Earn their trust.</span><span>We go underneath the loudest protectors to what they're guarding. This is where the grip starts to loosen, and where you notice yourself choosing rather than reacting.</span></li>
          <li><span class="label">Month three</span><span class="arc__title">Lead from Self.</span><span>We take it into the places that matter, like the conversation you've avoided, the way you run the leadership team, and how you show up at home. Then we build what keeps it going once we finish.</span></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap section split">
      <div class="stack"><p class="label">03 — Investment</p><h2 class="h2">Pricing, <em>plainly.</em></h2></div>
      <div class="split__body">
        <p>Fees depend on the shape of the engagement and who's paying, you or your company. I'm happy to talk numbers on our first call, and you'll have them in writing before you decide anything.</p>
        <p>Corporate invoicing is available. Some leaders fund this themselves and keep it entirely private. That's common, and it's your call.</p>
        <p><a class="btn" href="/contact/">Contact me for pricing</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="tone-stone">
    <div class="wrap section split">
      <div class="stack"><p class="label">04 — Fit</p><h2 class="h2">Is this <em>right for you?</em></h2></div>
      <div class="split__body fit">
        <div>
          <p class="label">Likely a good fit if</p>
          <ul class="rules">
            <li>You're doing well on paper and paying for it somewhere else</li>
            <li>You keep running into the same pattern, however much you understand it</li>
            <li>You're stepping into a bigger role, or out of one</li>
            <li>You'd rather look at what's driving you than learn another technique</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="label">Probably not if</p>
          <ul class="rules">
            <li>You've been sent and don't want to be here</li>
            <li>You want a 360 review or a skills course</li>
            <li>You're in crisis and need clinical support first. Tell me, and I'll help you find it</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Final heading="Start with" em="twenty minutes." text="No preparation needed. Bring whatever's most alive for you right now, and we'll see whether this is the right work at the right time." />
</Base>

<style>
  .wm-hero { padding-block: clamp(88px, 12vw, 160px); }
  .wm-hero > * { max-width: 860px; }
  .arc { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; counter-reset: none; }
  .arc li { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px; padding: 22px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--stone-rule); }
  .arc li:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--stone-rule); }
  .arc__title { font-family: var(--serif); font-size: clamp(28px, 2.6vw, 36px); line-height: 1.1; }
  .fit { gap: 36px; }
  .fit .label { margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .fit .rules li { border-color: var(--stone-rule); }
</style>
